sam: Heads up 1: we should lock down a pragmatic fetch strategy for the JS SDK today. Node <18, Node >=18, serverless (lambda), and edge runtimes need different guidance.

rachel: Agree. TL;DR: prefer global fetch when present, fall back to optional undici at runtime, and expose a tiny type + config for consumers to supply their own fetch.

tom: Proposed runtime code (avoid bundlers resolving undici at build):
```js
// get-fetch.mjs
export async function getFetch() {
  if (typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function') return globalThis.fetch;
  // guard to stop bundlers from eagerly replacing the dynamic import
  if (typeof process !== 'undefined') {
    const u = await import('undici');
    return u.fetch;
  }
  throw new Error('fetch not available in this runtime');
}
```
This keeps ESM edge builds small because they won't include undici.

izzy: For CJS consumers who call require() synchronously, add a tiny CJS shim that lazy-requires undici only when needed. Example: 
```js
// get-fetch.cjs
function getFetchSync() {
  if (typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function') return globalThis.fetch;
  // only require when called
  const { fetch } = require('undici');
  return fetch;
}
module.exports = { getFetchSync };
```
And document that SDK internals will always call the async helper so both worlds are supported.

rachel: Packaging notes: use conditional exports so Node ESM gets the .mjs entry and CJS gets .cjs. Also publish the runtime helpers at top-level of the package so advanced users can import them directly.

tom: Bundler caveat: Vite/Rollup may still try to statically analyze dynamic imports. Recommend the runtime check for globalThis.fetch BEFORE any import('undici') appears in code, and in docs call out pattern to avoid build-time hoisting.

izzy: Types: SDK should export a FetchLike alias so users don't need to change tsconfig. Eg: `export type FetchLike = (input: RequestInfo, init?: RequestInit) => Promise<Response>;` Add examples for tsconfig variations: Node-only app (add lib: ["es2020"]) and browser-facing app (add "dom").

rachel: Also document conflicts: `@types/node` can declare a different fetch signature in newer versions; recommend pinning `@types/node` < 20 or use the SDK's FetchLike type when passing custom fetch.

tom: Retries: default to no automatic retry for streaming/generation endpoints. For non-streaming read-only endpoints (embeddings, metadata GETs), provide opt-in retry with default strategy: retries=2, backoffMs=200, jitter=true, retryOn=[network errors, 502, 503, 504]. Make retry pluggable so integrators can swap in circuit-breakers.

izzy: UX: print a single dev-only warning on first fallback to undici: `console.warn('[redwood-inference-sdk] no global fetch detected 1 falling back to undici. Install undici or run Node >=18 for better compatibility. Set REDWOOD_SDK_SILENCE_FETCH_WARN=1 to hide.')` Keep it gated by NODE_ENV!== 'production' or env var.

rachel: Quickstart snippets for README: three copy-paste recipes: Edge (no deps), Node >=18 (no deps), Node <18 (npm i undici and optional env var).

Example:```md
# Node < 18
npm install undici
# optional: tell SDK to prefer the installed polyfill
export REDWOOD_SDK_FETCH=undici
```

sam: CI/tests: add matrix entries for node16, node18, deno, cloudflare-workers, vercel-edge. Small harness should assert getFetch returns callable and that SDK behaves when fetch is missing (falls back and logs once).

ci-bot: CI note: added node16 job but it timed out once due to network flakiness. We should mock network for fallback logic tests. build/237-fallback-tests shows the timeout.

izzy: Docs page checklist I can PR: code samples (mjs + cjs), tsconfig examples, FetchLike export, retry policy doc, bundler pitfalls, env vars list, one-line troubleshooting.

sam: Perfect. Keep code examples verbatim in repo so we can link to them from docs. I'll file the SDK RFC and include the tests matrix. Thanks all.
